    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "`build_client` is now implemented in `app/llm_client.py` and meets all four requirements. The existing test passes (`pytest -q`: 1 passed). I also ran a quick check using a stub transport that returns one 500 error and then a 200, and it confirmed each requirement.\n\n**One thing you might not expect:** openai 3.19.2 uses the **`httpx2`** package, not `httpx`, and `httpx2` isn't installed in `.venv`. So the code imports `httpx2`, which openai already brings in, and I added no dependencies.\n\n**How each requirement is met:**\n1. **Timeouts:** `httpx2.Timeout(30.0, connect=5.0)` gives connect 5s and read, write and pool 30s. I set it on both the HTTP client and `OpenAI(timeout=...)`, because the SDK attaches its own timeout to every request and would otherwise override the HTTP client's setting.\n2. **Retries:** `max_retries=2`.\n3. **Logging:** a `\"request\"` event hook logs `\"%s %s\" % (method, url)` at INFO on the `app.http` logger. The hook runs on every send, so retries get logged too. In the check, the failed first attempt and the retry each logged `GET https://api.openai.com/v1/models`.\n4. **Transport:** `transport` is passed straight to the HTTP client, and the stub transport received both requests. I built the HTTP client with openai's `DefaultHttpxClient`, so openai's other defaults (connection limits, following redirects) still apply.\n\n**Note:** the check ran from a scratch file, `_smoke.py`, in the project root. I wasn't allowed to delete it, so please remove it yourself."
  },
